<title>FRANCE: France sells 24.23 bln Ffr OATs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 24.23 bln Ffr OATs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury sold the following government bonds (OATs) at auction on Thursday.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 25.APR.07	5.50	 14.930 BLN	  5.56</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 38.400 BLN/2.6		   NIL		 99.52</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 60.0						    25.MAR</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							   03.APR</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 25.JAN.09  N/A (TEC 10)    9.295 BLN	    N/A</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 23.795 BLN/2.4		  245 MLN	   101.88</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 100.0						   25.MAR</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT OFFER</p>
<p>							    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 23 to 25 billion francs of OATs in total. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 2.6.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
